{
  "name": "How to Prepare Your Log Home for Refinishing",
  "step": [
    {
      "name": "Step 1",
      "text": "Getting your log home ready for refinishing is crucial for a lasting and beautiful result. It’s more than just slapping on a new coat of stain! First up, you need a thorough inspection. Take a good look for any signs of rot, insect damage, or failures in your chinking and seals. You want to address these issues before you even think about applying new finish. Next, a really good cleaning is essential. You can't just refinish over dirt and grime; the new stain won't stick properly. After cleaning, you might need to remove any old, failing finish. Sometimes this means sanding or using a stripper, but it depends on the condition of the logs. Once it's clean and prepped, you can move on to repairs. This includes things like fixing any damaged logs, re-chinking, or sealing up any gaps. Only then are you ready for the new stain or finish. Remember, the weather plays a big role here, as you need dry conditions for application and curing. If you’re dealing with extensive damage, or just aren’t sure about the best way to tackle the prep work, a professional can step in and make sure it’s done right. We can help you through each of these steps!",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 1
    }
  ],
